real-time, analyzing workload requirements and intelligently adjusting CPU and memory allocations without service disruption — delivering up to 80% infrastructure cost savings while maintaining application performance.", "score": 0.71185225, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.sherweb.com/blog/cloud-server/aws-azure-google-cloud-pricing-comparison/", "title": "Cloud pricing comparison: AWS vs. Azure vs. GCP - Sherweb", "content": "# Cloud pricing comparison: AWS vs. There are several factors to consider when choosing a suitable cloud service vendor, with pricing chief among them. Most of us recognize Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Amazon Web Services (AWS) as major leaders in the space, but which one is best for your cloud business? ## **AWS****, Azure and GCP cloud pricing comparison**. Azure, AWS and GCP all have their own pricing calculators, as well as different naming conventions for their respective services. Microsoft Azure has a significantly more robust lineup of compute products to choose from, including but not limited to Virtual Machines, Azure Virtual Desktop and Azure Service Fabric. Because of all the variables involved, it can be an arduous process going through each platform’s cost calculator to compare specific pricing, whether it’s for cloud computing, cloud storage or some other environment. **Even when calculating costs at scale, it’s easy to see that cloud pricing ultimately depends on what type of instance you want, on what kind of server and where.", "score": 0.70750624, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://medium.com/@bohdan.vasylkiv/aws-vs-gcp-vs-azure-what-about-prices-749bd169d6a9", "title": "AWS vs GCP vs Azure: What about prices? | by Bohdan Vasylkiv", "content": "Azure VM is marginally less expensive than AWS, costing $12.05 for US West, $10.11 for US East, and $11.42 for the London-based service. At the", "score": 0.70483154, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://softwaremind.com/blog/aws-azure-and-google-price-comparison/", "title": "AWS, Azure, and Google Price Comparison - Cloud - Software Mind", "content": "When conducting an AWS, Azure, or Google price comparison, it’s essential to understand the key factors influencing cloud costs, including computing, storage, networking, and additional services. Meanwhile, Google Cloud stands out for its innovative pricing strategies, such as sustained use discounts and preemptible VM instances, which make it a cost-effective option for analytics-heavy workloads and Cloud BI solutions. Generally, Google Cloud has lower pricing for analytics-heavy workloads and sustained use, but AWS offers cost-effective options for diverse and global services. When evaluating cloud storage pricing and computing capabilities among AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud Platform (GCP), you must consider each provider’s unique offerings and how they align with your organization’s needs. To recap, pricing plays a crucial role in comparing AWS, Google Cloud, and Azure, but businesses must also weigh factors like ease of use, service availability, and ecosystem compatibility. AWS is feature-rich, Azure integrates with Microsoft, and Google Cloud is cost-efficient.", "score": 0.6994397, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.effectivesoft.com/blog/cloud-pricing-comparison.html", "title": "Cloud pricing comparison - AWS, Azure, GCP, Oracle - EffectiveSoft", "content": "In this article, we provide an overview of the prices for computing and storage services provided by the global cloud giants—Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Provider (GCP), and Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI). | Pricing models | Pay-as-you-go, Saving Plans, Dedicated Hosts, Reserved Instances, Dedicated Hosts | Pay-as-you-go, Saving Plan, Reserved Instances, Hybrid Benefit, Spot Instances, Azure Dev/Test | Pay-as-you-go, Committed Use | Pay-as-you-go, Universal Credits, Monthly Universal Credits, Annual Universal Credits, Bring Your Own License, Oracle Cloud at Customer, Government Subscriptions |. * AWS, Azure, OCI, and GCP all offer pricing models that allow users to commit to a certain usage for a discounted rate. For savings plans with a one-year commitment across different configurations, AWS generally offers the lowest prices compared to Azure and GCP. To compare the storage costs of the four providers, we analyzed the prices of the S3 (AWS), Blob Storage (Azure), Cloud Storage (GCP), and Object Storage (OCI) services.", "score": 0.6638657, "raw_content": null}], "response_time": 0.88, "request_id": "6d380b03-0179-4b7d-9f5e-7b0b0317473b"}, {"query": "mejores prácticas multi-cloud CI/CD", "follow_up_questions": null, "answer": null, "images": [], "results": [{"url": "https://www.cloudthat.com/resources/blog/ci-cd-in-multi-cloud-environments-challenges-and-best-practices/", "title": "CI/CD in Multi-Cloud Environments: Challenges and Best Practices", "content": "1. **Tooling Incompatibility:** Different cloud platforms often come with their own native CI/CD tools, like Azure DevOps, AWS CodePipeline, and Google Cloud Build. While these tools are optimized for their respective environments, integrating them into a cohesive CI/CD pipeline across multiple clouds can be difficult due to differences in workflows, APIs, and automation capabilities. 2. **Security and Compliance:** Managing security in a multi-cloud CI/CD pipeline is complex due to the need to enforce consistent security policies across disparate platforms. 4. **Use Multi-Cloud Orchestration Tools:** Employ multi-cloud orchestration tools like Spinnaker or Argo CD to manage and automate CI/CD workflows across different cloud environments. Implementing CI/CD pipelines in a multi-cloud environment is undoubtedly challenging, but with the right strategies and tools, these challenges can be effectively managed. By adopting a unified toolset, embracing infrastructure as code, centralizing security management, and using specialized orchestration tools, organizations can build robust, efficient, and secure CI/CD pipelines that span multiple cloud platforms.", "score": 0.9999374, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/devops/comments/13c88ix/multi_service_cicd_best_practices/?tl=es-419", "title": "Mejores prácticas de CI/CD para múltiples servicios : r/devops - Reddit", "content": "En general, la mejor práctica es solo probar / construir / desplegar la parte que realmente ha cambiado. Esto es un poco más fácil si divides", "score": 0.99992394, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://circleci.com/blog/ci-cd-requirements-for-multi-cloud/", "title": "CI/CD requirements for multi-cloud - CircleCI", "content": "CI/CD for multi-cloud environments requires sophisticated orchestration and standardization across different cloud providers. Unlike single-cloud deployments, multi-cloud strategies demand a unified CI/CD pipeline that can handle varying provider APIs, security models, and deployment patterns. * **Provider-specific configurations** – Each cloud provider requires unique deployment configurations and infrastructure definitions. * **Complex security management** – Security policies and compliance must be maintained across multiple provider environments. * **Cross-cloud networking** – Managing connectivity and data transfer between cloud providers adds complexity. Testing multi-cloud deployments requires attention to provider-specific behaviors:. * **Cross-cloud integration testing** – Verify interactions between services on different providers. * **Centralize identity management** – Implement single sign-on across cloud providers. CircleCI provides the sophisticated tooling needed for modern multi-cloud development and deployment. * **Native provider integrations** – Deploy to any major cloud provider. With continuous delivery becoming essential for multi-cloud success, CircleCI offers the robust foundation teams need to automate, scale, and optimize their deployment pipelines across any cloud provider.", "score": 0.99987364, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://forums.suse.com/t/what-are-the-best-practices-for-implementing-ci-cd-pipelines-in-a-multi-cloud-environment-and-how-do-you-ensure-security-across-different-platforms/44157", "title": "What are the best practices for implementing CI/CD pipelines in a ...", "content": "In a multi-cloud CI/CD setup, use a centralized secrets manager (e.g., HashiCorp Vault) for secure secret handling, enforce compliance with", "score": 0.9998591, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://hokstadconsulting.com/blog/best-practices-multi-cloud-ci-cd-pipelines", "title": "Best Practices for Multi-Cloud CI/CD Pipelines | Hokstad Consulting", "content": "Multi-cloud CI/CD pipelines allow organisations to automate building, testing, and deploying applications across multiple cloud providers like AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud. By addressing these challenges with standardised tools, efficient workflows, and robust security practices, organisations can optimise multi-cloud pipelines for performance and cost-efficiency. Tools like **Terraform** and **Pulumi** make it possible to manage infrastructure consistently across different cloud APIs. By defining resources in version-controlled files, you can maintain uniform configurations across AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud. Once you\'ve established standardised CI/CD pipelines and Infrastructure as Code (IaC) practices, the next step in a multi-cloud strategy is ensuring robust security and observability. Their services focus on creating automated CI/CD pipelines optimised for multi-cloud setups, often achieving expense reductions of **30–50%** through strategic resource management and cost engineering. Managing fragmented tools in multi-cloud CI/CD pipelines can be challenging, but there are ways to simplify and unify processes across different environments. To manage costs effectively in multi-cloud CI/CD pipelines, businesses should prioritise **resource efficiency** and **automation**.", "score": 0.99983656