vice – in the world of SaaS onboarding metrics, this is the customers’ “aha moment.” Of course, the sooner your customers realize the value you add to their business, the better off you are, as this will reduce other negative metrics like customer churn. * **How do you measure Onboarding Completion Rate?** Divide the total number of customers who completed a task or process by the total number of onboarded customers in that time period. The ROI of Onboarding metric tracks the relate revenue per customer to costs. What are customer onboarding metrics?", "score": 0.9807288, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/microsoftsentinelblog/automating-the-onboarding-on-premises-aws-and-gcp-vms-on-sentinel-with-azure-arc/1488267", "title": "Automating the onboarding on-premises, AWS and GCP ...", "content": "On this article we will focus on how you can not only automate the MMA installation using extensions but also leveraging Azure Policies.", "score": 0.9697854, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wx_LAHdZ2P0", "title": "Deploying Agents: AWS vs Azure vs GCP (Real-World ...", "content": "In this video I\'ll give you a complete comparison between the AWS Azour and GCP.", "score": 0.9390248, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/monitoring/api/metrics_gcp", "title": "Google Cloud metrics overview | Cloud Monitoring", "content": "# Google Cloud metrics overview Stay organized with collections Save and categorize content based on your preferences. Cloud Monitoring supports the metric types defined by Google Cloud services. The following pages display the metric types for a subset of Google Cloud services. The name of a metric type identifies the associated service. For example, metric types whose name starts with `compute.googleapis.com/` are assigned to the `compute` service:. * Metric types: A through B. + For Cloud Run functions that rely on the `run.googleapis.com` API, the metric types are generated by Cloud Run. For a list of metric types, see `run`. + **Cloud Endpoints**: APIs managed by Cloud Endpoints write  `serviceruntime` metrics against the `api` monitored-resource type. + The prefix `container.googleapis.com` is for older Google Kubernetes Engine metric types. For newer GKE metric types, see the `kubernetes.io` metrics. * Metric types: D through H. * Metric types: I through O. The VM Manager generates metrics with the `osconfig.googleapis.com` prefix. * Metric types: P through Z.", "score": 0.79692537, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.proteus.co/insights/view/1919-13-metrics-for-executives-in-customer-onboarding", "title": "13 Key Metrics in Customer Onboarding For Executive ...", "content": "# 13 Key Metrics For Executive Teams in Customer Onboarding. For customers, the onboarding process is their first real experience of the product or service they’ve invested in. Metrics such as customer churn rate during and post-onboarding help your team identify where the quickest time to value is needed. * When it comes to B2B customer onboarding, the metrics that matter most are those that ensure long-term success and customer satisfaction. ### Metrics for B2B Customer Onboarding Success. Why It Matters: A strong NPS reflects confidence in the product and a positive customer onboarding experience. Why It Matters: High engagement during onboarding signals that customers are actively learning and adopting the product. Why It Matters: A high referral rate indicates that customers are satisfied and confident enough in the product to recommend it to others, a clear sign of success in the customer onboarding experience. Why It Matters: This metric demonstrates how effectively onboarding fosters deeper customer engagement with the product.", "score": 0.7505527, "raw_content": null}], "response_time": 0.98, "request_id": "8ec1f6c7-ac8d-4d48-9e60-5bdc370d3cbc"}, {"query": "costes ocultos cloud providers análisis", "follow_up_questions": null, "answer": null, "images": [], "results": [{"url": "https://bluemarasolutions.com/costes-ocultos-de-la-adopcion-de-la-nube/", "title": "¿Cuáles son los costes ocultos de la adopción de la nube? - Bluemara", "content": "Para analizar el verdadero coste de la adopción de la nube, la tarifa de suscripción mensual por sí sola no representa una imagen completa y las organizaciones deben evaluar los gastos asociados, los precios con respecto al consumo real del servicio (que puede ser impredecible) y los gastos imprevistos incurridos debido a las políticas de los proveedores o la situación de uso. Las organizaciones que no identifican la mejor opción de precios y el paquete de servicios para sus casos de uso específicos, un presupuesto ajustado y los requisitos comerciales, pueden no ser capaces de optar por la opción más viable financieramente. * ***Soporte:***\xa0incluso con grandes proveedores de servicios en la nube, el servicio de soporte inmediato puede no ser una opción para todos los clientes debido a las limitaciones de su fuerza laboral y su creciente base de clientes.", "score": 0.709684, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.computing.es/cloud/los-costes-ocultos-del-cloud-computing/", "title": "Los costes ocultos del cloud computing", "content": "Un consejo general es analizar los costes (todos) en relación con cada uno de mis servicios, en ambos escenarios, para poder decidir”.", "score": 0.6490677, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://revistabyte.es/actualidad-it/costes-ocultos-del-cloud-computing/", "title": "Costes ocultos del cloud computing: optimizar la factura - Byte TI", "content": "Los costes ocultos del cloud aparecen cuando la organización se centra en el precio del servicio (compute, almacenamiento, bases de datos) pero", "score": 0.6241337, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.inmoveit.com/costes-ocultos-en-la-migracion-al-cloud-como-evitarlos/", "title": "Costes ocultos en la migración al Cloud: Cómo evitarlos", "content": "Los costes ocultos son aquellos gastos que no suelen incluirse en el presupuesto inicial de migración. Pueden surgir por: ... Si no se controlan, estos costes", "score": 0.51969254, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.channelpartner.es/whitepapers/los-costes-ocultos-del-cloud/", "title": "Los costes ocultos del cloud | Channel Partner", "content": "Pero no se trata de un camino de rosas, pues existen costes ocultos y problemas que pueden surgir sobre la marcha y que pueden dar por tierra un proyecto.", "score": 0.3813814, "raw_content": null}], "response_time": 1.26, "request_id": "3d71e71c-9fbc-490e-96b1-af7e84a4aa34"}, {"query": "casos estudio multi-cloud IaC", "follow_up_questions": null, "answer": null, "images": [], "results": [{"url": "https://medium.com/atmosly/implementing-iac-in-a-multi-cloud-environment-393df3d0f7d2", "title": "Implementing IAC in a Multi-Cloud Environment | Atmosly - Medium", "content": "By defining infrastructure through code, IaC enables organizations to manage their multi-cloud environments consistently and efficiently. IaC", "score": 0.9999931, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/391012996_Infrastructure_as_Code_IaC_Best_Practices_in_Multi-Cloud_Environments", "title": "Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Best Practices in Multi-Cloud ...", "content": "This research paper delves deeply into the best practices for implementing IaC in multi-cloud environments, addressing challenges of consistency", "score": 0.9999821, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://dzone.com/articles/iac-multi-cloud-consistency-security", "title": "Infrastructure as Code (IaC) in a Multi-Cloud Environment - DZone", "content": "The aim of this research is to identify and analyze the main challenges associated with using IaC in a multi-cloud setting, as well as to", "score": 0.9999349, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.academicpublishers.org/journals/index.php/ijns/article/view/5120", "title": "Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Best Practices for Multi-Cloud ...", "content": "# Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Best Practices for Multi-Cloud Deployments in Enterprises. This article provides a complete examination of IaC best practices for multi-cloud settings, focusing on modular architecture, tool standardization, governance, security integration, and automation via CI/CD pipelines. Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, and policy-as-code frameworks like OPA are all appraised for their use in cross-cloud orchestration. These insights are intended to assist DevOps and cloud engineering teams in creating durable, scalable, and secure multi-cloud infrastructures. This article provides a complete examination of IaC best practices for multi-cloud settings, focusing on modular architecture, tool standardization, governance, security integration, and automation via CI/CD pipelines. These insights are intended to assist DevOps and cloud engineering teams in creating durable, scalable, and secure multi-cloud infrastructures. Infrastructure as Code, Multi-Cloud, Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, Enterprise Cloud Governance, DevOps Automation, Configuration Management, Policy-as-Code, CI/CD Integration, Immutable Infrastructure. Configuration Drift Detection in IaC for Multi-Cloud Systems. Configuration Drift Detection in IaC for Multi-Cloud Systems.", "score": 0.99986756, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://nareshit.com/blogs/infrastructure-as-code-iac-best-practices-in-multi-cloud", "title": "Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Best Practices for Multi-Cloud | DevOps", "content": "Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Best Practices in Multi-Cloud. # **Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Best Practices in Multi-Cloud:**. This is where Infrastructure as Code (IaC) becomes the backbone of multi-cloud operations. With IaC, DevOps teams can create repeatable, automated, and version-controlled environments across multiple clouds improving speed, consistency, and reliability. For DevOps engineers, IaC is the key to multi-cloud agility enabling fast 