e/). + [up](/docs/iac/cli/commands/pulumi_up/). + [version](/docs/iac/cli/commands/pulumi_version/). + [watch](/docs/iac/cli/commands/pulumi_watch/). + [whoami](/docs/iac/cli/commands/pulumi_whoami/). + [Introduction](/docs/iac/comparisons/terraform/). + [Pulumi terminology](/docs/iac/comparisons/terraform/terminology/). * [Integrate with Pulumi IaC](/docs/esc/guides/integrate-with-pulumi-iac/). - [Introduction](/docs/esc/integrations/infrastructure/pulumi-iac/). - [pulumi-stacks](/docs/esc/integrations/infrastructure/pulumi-iac/pulumi-stacks/). * [Pulumi CLI](/docs/iac/cli/). 2. [Infrastructure as Code](/docs/iac/). * [Edit this Page](https://github.com/pulumi/docs/edit/master/content/docs/iac/comparisons/terraform/_index.md). For advanced use cases, it is possible to [use Pulumi IaC without Pulumi Cloud](/docs/support/faq#can-i-use-pulumi-without-depending-on-the-/pulumi-cloud/), which works a lot more like Terraform, but requires you to manage state and concurrency issues. * [Edit this Page](https://github.com/pulumi/docs/edit/master/content/docs/iac/comparisons/terraform/_index.md).", "score": 0.61779, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://softwarelogic.co/en/blog/7-key-differences-terraform-vs-pulumi-for-multi-cloud-in-2026/", "title": "7 Key Differences: Terraform vs Pulumi for Multi-Cloud 2026", "content": "# 7 Key Differences: Terraform vs Pulumi for Multi-Cloud in 2026. 7 Key Differences: Terraform vs Pulumi for Multi-Cloud in 2026. How do Terraform and Pulumi compare for multi-cloud deployments in 2026? **Choosing the right Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool is crucial for successful multi-cloud deployments in 2026.** As organizations increasingly embrace complex, distributed architectures, the debate between **Terraform** and **Pulumi** intensifies. In this comprehensive guide, we’ll compare **Terraform** and **Pulumi** across seven key dimensions that matter most for DevOps and cloud teams. **Pulumi** also supports multi-cloud, and its language-first approach makes it easy to abstract over cloud differences. A development team uses **Pulumi** to deploy serverless functions on AWS Lambda and Google Cloud Functions, handling environment-specific logic with TypeScript. **Both Terraform and Pulumi are excellent Infrastructure as Code tools for multi-cloud deployments in 2026.** Your choice depends on your team’s skills, provider needs, and workflow preferences:. 7 Key Differences: Terraform vs Pulumi for Multi-Cloud 2026.", "score": 0.53269315, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/improwised-technologies_pulumi-vs-terraform-best-iac-tool-for-2025-activity-7392147963445387264-WE5L", "title": "Terraform vs Pulumi: Which IaC tool boosts your cloud ROI? - LinkedIn", "content": "🚀 #Terraform Commands Every DevOps & SRE Engineer Should Know ⚙️ Terraform helps you automate cloud infrastructure — and mastering these commands is key to managing your infra like a pro 👇 Setup & Initialization terraform init Initializes Terraform, downloads required providers & sets up backend. “From code commit to live metrics — all fully automated on AWS 🚀” I recently wrapped up my end-to-end Multi-Tenant SaaS project (MyDaily SaaS) — designed to simulate a real-world cloud production setup with CI/CD, Kubernetes, Infrastructure as Code, and full observability. Key advantages: ⚡ Multi-stage YAML pipelines 🐳 Deep Docker & Kubernetes integration 🔐 Built-in DevSecOps (scans, code quality, security gates) 🌩️ Works with any language, any cloud 🧩 Enterprise-grade governance & RBAC If your team is moving toward cloud-native engineering, Azure Pipelines is not just a CI/CD tool — it’s a strategic accelerator for modern DevOps. Read our blog: https://lnkd.in/gUfjQu3S #Azure #AzureDevOps #CICD #CloudNative #DevOps #AzurePipelines #Kubernetes #Containers #DevSecOps #CloudComputing #Automation #AKS #SrijayaramInfotech.", "score": 0.5255399, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://stackgen.com/blog/terraform-vs-pulumi-vs-cdk", "title": "Terraform vs. Pulumi vs. AWS CDK: Choosing the Right IaC Tool", "content": "Terraform, Pulumi, and AWS CDK all solve the same core problem: defining and provisioning cloud infrastructure as code, but they fit different teams, pressures, and cloud strategies in very different ways. When your security team mandates policy enforcement, and an auditor wants to know who approved an infrastructure change six months ago, Terraform\'s enterprise tooling has a credible, documented answer. If the current IaC cost is a pressure point, model the total cost of ownership honestly: OSS Terraform with self-managed state in S3, Pulumi Open Source with Pulumi Cloud, and CDK (if AWS-only) all look very different from Terraform Enterprise at renewal time. If you\'re a **Pulumi or CDK team**, Aiden works natively with your language stack, generating TypeScript or Python infrastructure code that passes your existing tests and meets your compliance requirements before it ever reaches review. * **Pulumi** — developer-heavy teams wanting real-language IaC with built-in policy-as-code; best for multi-cloud with fast-moving dev teams.", "score": 0.52510154, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://www.pulumi.com/blog/all-iac-including-terraform-and-hcl/", "title": "Pulumi for All Your IaC — Including Terraform and HCL", "content": "First, Pulumi Cloud will support Terraform and OpenTofu, so you can continue using any Terraform or Pulumi CLI and language with the complete Pulumi Cloud product, including our infrastructure engineering AI agent, Neo. Second, Pulumi’s own open source IaC tool will support HCL natively as one of its many languages, alongside the industry’s best languages including Python, TypeScript, Go, C#, Java, and YAML. Pulumi has always been two things: Pulumi IaC, the multi-language, open source infrastructure as code technology, and Pulumi Cloud, our commercial platform that includes infrastructure state management and visibility, our AI agent Neo, secrets management, policy as code, governance, and much more. This is explicitly not meant to be a lift-and-shift migration option – we have many other techniques for that, including the new Terraform support in Pulumi Cloud – but is instead for teammates who are more comfortable with or prefer HCL over general-purpose languages, but still want to leverage the more modern Pulumi IaC engine with its advanced multi-language capabilities.", "score": 0.4746074, "raw_content": null}], "response_time": 1.06, "request_id": "0351d04d-cc78-4d4a-8573-c2e49593a06f"}, {"query": "Herramientas testing IaC Terratest Checkov ejemplos", "follow_up_questions": null, "answer": null, "images": [], "results": [{"url": "https://www.infracloud.io/blogs/testing-iac-terratest/", "title": "Testing your Infrastructure as Code using Terratest - InfraCloud", "content": "Testing your Infrastructure as Code using Terratest. # Testing your Infrastructure as Code using Terratest. ## Testing infrastructure code. Terratest is a Go library developed by Gruntwork that helps you create and automate tests for your Infra as Code written with Terraform, Packer for IaaS providers like Amazon, Google, or for a Kubernetes cluster. Terratest executes sanity and functional testing for your Infrastructure code. We can also leverage Terratest for compliance testing of your infrastructure, for example, to have versioning and encryption enabled on any new S3 bucket created through your IaC. Now we will execute some integration tests using terratest. Terratest takes the output from Terraform’s `output.tf` as input for its tests. package terratest import(\\"testing\\"\\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\\"\\"github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/modules/terraform\\"). As you can see it has executed our test function `TestApiGateway`, in which it has performed HTTP GET test on `deployment_invoke_url` of API Gateway and returned test status. We have created our own test function for Authorizer using Terratest and AWS Go SDK methods.", "score": 0.9999542, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://medium.com/@kaliarch/terratest-a-comprehensive-guide-to-testing-infrastructure-as-code-iac-0323eb56cc52", "title": "Terratest: A Comprehensive Guide to Testing Infrastructure as Code ...", "content": "Create two directories: examples (for IaC code) and test (for Terratest scripts). · Clone a basic Terraform example into the examples directory.", "score": 0.99992037, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://dev.to/team3/applying-the-sast-tool-checkov-to-a-terraform-iac-project-1l23", "title": "Applying the SAST Tool Checkov to a Terraform IaC Project", "content": "In this article, we will use Checkov, a SAST tool designed for IaC, to scan a small Terraform project and identify security issues.", "score": 0.99983656, "raw_content": null}, {"url": "https://terratest.gruntwork.io/", "title": "Terratest | Automated tests for your infrastructure code.", "content": "# **Automated tests** for your infrastructure code. Terratest is a Go library that provides patterns and helper functions for testing infrastructure, with 1st-class support for Terraform, Packer, Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, GCP, and more. ## Test infrastructure code with Terratest **in 4 steps**. Use Terratest to deploy infrastructure. Use Terratest to execute your real IaC tools (e.g., Terraform, Packer, etc.) to deploy real infrastructure (e.g., servers) in a real environment (e.g., AWS). ## **Test** with Terratest. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/examples/terraform-hello-world-example/main.tf. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/test/terraform\\\\_hello\\\\_world\\\\_example\\\\_test.go. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/examples/packer-hello-world-example/build.pkr.hcl. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/test/packer\\\\_hello\\\\_world\\\\_example\\\\_test.go. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/examples/docker-hello-world-example/Dockerfile. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/test/docker\\\\_hello\\\\_world\\\\_example\\\\_test.go. github.com/gruntwork-io/terratest/